# Tests serve the product

Canonical: `docs/TESTING.md`.

## Do

- Treat a failing test/smoke as a signal to fix **product**, **environment**, or a **wrong test**
- Keep requirements that docs demand (tax at gateway, real auth, paid activation, webhooks, etc.) even when a sandbox check is red
- Label harnesses honestly (`mock-only`, local-only); never report them as gateway/store ready
- Delete bogus tests that only exist to look green while intent is unmet

## Do not

- Disable, stub, or omit product behavior (e.g. Stripe `automatic_tax`, auth, payment checks) so a smoke/unit test passes
- Default public sites/APIs to unpaid mock activate to clear E2E
- Soften assertions, `#[ignore]` requirement tests, or rewrite docs to excuse a bypass
- Adapt the app to the test; adapt the test to real intent — or remove the test

## Incident reminder

2026-11-23: removing Stripe Tax so Checkout smoke passed was **unacceptable**. Tax was restored. Fail closed until Tax (or an equivalent tax-capable gateway path) actually works.
